 is evidence for that: 173 lines left embeddings.js, a whole cross-encoder module went, the thread count halved, and the blocking fact did not move. Rejected rather than 'propose the bridge upstream' because the inbound bridge, specified in the report, would if granted in full still deliver a CPU-only embedder. WHAT IS NOT REJECTED, and it changes the shape of this ticket's ownership question: #6012 already routes PASSAGES outbound to an external endpoint (pref embeddings.endpoint, TEI wire shape, embeddings.js:1027-1053 and :952-970), so Zotero is a candidate CONSUMER of the facility, not only a candidate provider. A facility zoteus owns can serve both -- one model on the machine per the 2026-09-02 ruling -- while staying a native process that reaches CUDA. The gain is partial: embedQuery never consults the pref, so Zotero still loads its own engine for queries; the saving is on the indexing pass. Hardening that hook (declare the pref, send model/dimension, verify the returned shape) is a small upstream filing that belongs to GOVERNANCE.md's queue, not to this outcome. Report: verification/BRIDGE-0496.md
